From 8bf5380b123aa952e019ad859707581033830274 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Kocsis <kocsisadam1991@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 09:23:04 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Add batched fixed-width recognition and session profiling
 hooks

Upstream calls Session::Run once per detected region at a width that changes
with every crop. getTextLinesBatched packs regions into one [N,3,48,W] run and
pads with post-normalisation zero, which is what PaddleOCR does at imgW=320.

Measured on the game-capture-1080p fixture, 30 warm runs: CPU 89.6 -> 83.2 ms
p50. The same patch is what makes DirectML viable at all (164 -> 38 ms), which
matters if the GPU provider is revived.

Known limit, same as PaddleOCR's: a region wider than the target aspect ratio
is squashed rather than bucketed. Fine for dialogue crops, worth revisiting for
full-width subtitles.

enableProfiling/endProfiling expose ONNX Runtime's profile JSON so provider
placement can be verified instead of assumed.
